A 2026 twelve-person pilot also closely matches your rollout. It found that TraceDesk required more configuration and that occasional users considered its forms heavy, but its workflow advantage became more important over several weeks than it appeared during the initial demonstration. Since most of your team is new to both tools, Boardly’s familiarity advantage applies mainly to you rather than to the whole group.

The trade-off is real: by choosing TraceDesk, you give up Boardly’s cleaner board, faster setup, and your own existing familiarity. Expect more preparation and onboarding. I would manage that by:

